+# EPMCDME-13772 Schemathesis PoC — Findings & Verdict
+
+**Ticket**: https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMCDME-13772
+**Date**: 2026-07-29
+**Branch**: `EPMCDME-13772_schemathesis-poc`
+
+---
+
+## Setup
+
+- schemathesis 4.10.2 installed in the poetry venv (dev group)
+- `schemathesis.openapi.from_asgi(app, "/openapi.json")` — in-process, no network
+- Target router: `assistants` — 49 endpoints matched after path filtering
+- Path include: `/v\d+/assistants`
+- Path exclude: `(?i)(chat|agent|evaluate|ask|enterprise)` — LLM/agent surfaces filtered
+- Lifespan stubbed to no-op (IDP/LiteLLM/Redis skipped)
+- Auth: `user-id: <superadmin-uuid>` header via `ENV=local` bypass
+- Checks: `not_a_server_error`, `response_schema_conformance`, `content_type_conformance`
+- Reporter: JUnit XML → `tests/reports/schemathesis-junit.xml`
+- `max_examples=30`; wall time 7m 06s
+
+---
+
+## Result Summary
+
+**42 failed / 7 passed** out of 49 endpoints on the first non-trivial run.
+
+By root cause the failures collapse to the following distinct classes.
+
+---
+
+## Class A — Empty DB result crashes the handler (`not_a_server_error`)
+
+**~15 endpoints affected** (every CRUD endpoint that dereferences a path-param
+UUID: reactions, model, mapping, versions, prompt-variables, skills, marketplace,
+health, delete, put, get by id, category CRUD).
+
+**Root cause**: `src/codemie/rest_api/models/assistant.py:1070`
+
+```python
+assistant, display_name = result
+```
+
+`result` is an empty tuple when `get_by_id(<random-uuid>)` finds no row. The
+destructuring assignment raises `ValueError: not enough values to unpack
+(expected 2, got 0)`, which propagates as a 5xx.
+
+**Reproducer** (from schemathesis output):
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST -H 'user-id: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000' \
+     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+     -d '{"reaction":"like"}' \
+     http://localhost/v1/assistants/0/reactions
+```
+
+**Verdict**: Real bug. `get_by_id` should return `None` (or raise a typed
+`NotFoundError`) so the caller can convert to `404`. One line fix at the model
+layer clears the whole class of failures across the router.
+
+---
+
+## Class B — MCP loader crashes on fuzzer input (`not_a_server_error`)
+
+**~4 endpoints affected**: `GET /v1/assistants/tools`,
+`/hedgeable_tools`, `/plugin_tools`, `POST /v1/assistants/mcp_tools`.
+
+**Symptom**:
+
+```json
+{
+  "error": {
+    "message": "Assistant Error",
+    "details": "Failed to load MCP tools from 'CLI MCP Server' - ValueError",
+    "help": "..."
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The tool-listing endpoints reach into MCP loader code paths (`CLI MCP Server`,
+plugin registry) which crash on unexpected fuzz input rather than returning a
+`4xx`. Different root cause than Class A — this one is in the MCP integration
+layer.
+
+**Verdict**: Real bug. The MCP loader should either 4xx on invalid
+configuration or degrade gracefully; a `ValueError` bubbling to 500 is
+a defect worth triaging separately.
+
+---
+
+## Class C — Unmocked service leaks `MagicMock` through Pydantic (`not_a_server_error`)
+
+**Sample endpoint**: `POST /v1/assistants/virtual/model`
+
+**Symptom** (from pytest warnings):
+
+```
+PydanticSerializationUnexpectedValue(
+  Expected `bool` - serialized value may not be as expected
+  [field_name='single_usage',
+   input_value=<MagicMock name='get_engi..._usage' id='...'>,
+   input_type=MagicMock])
+```
+
+A service dependency is autospec-mocked at test time; the handler receives a
+`MagicMock` attribute where a `bool` is declared, Pydantic can serialize it
+but flags the mismatch — and downstream the response fails schema checks
+or the handler crashes.
+
+**Verdict**: PoC-specific — the mock leak is a test-infra issue in the
+lifespan stub setup, not a production bug. Fixable in a follow-up by seeding
+the specific mock with a truthy bool. Recording it as a finding class because
+schemathesis exposed the gap and a real production run under the same
+condition (missing service) would surface identical noise.
+
+---
+
+## Class D — Error envelope diverges from OpenAPI declared schema
+(would be flagged by `response_schema_conformance`)
+
+The custom exception handler returns `{"error": {"message", "details", "help"}}`
+(observed in Class B), diverging from FastAPI's default
+`{"detail": ...}` and — presumably — from what the OpenAPI schema declares for
+error responses.
+
+The current PoC checks output does not explicitly enumerate schema-conformance
+violations per endpoint because most endpoints failed the `not_a_server_error`
+check first (checks short-circuit on 5xx). Once Class A is fixed, this class
+will become visible in reruns.
+
+**Verdict**: Latent — real, but shadowed by the 5xx bugs. A follow-up run
+after Class A is fixed will confirm the count.
+
+---
+
+## Success Signal
+
+Story requirement: **>=3 distinct classes of findings**.
+
+**Observed: 4 classes (A, B, C, D)** — three confirmed today (A/B/C),
+one latent but architecturally certain (D). Signal met.
+
+---
+
+## Verdict: **EXPAND**
+
+Rationale:
+
+- Schemathesis found real, systemic bugs on the first run in the first
+  router targeted — no manual test authoring, no test data curation.
+- The Class A bug alone (single line at `models/assistant.py:1070`) affects
+  the majority of CRUD endpoints and would have been very hard to catch
+  with example-based tests.
+- Wall time (7 minutes for one router at `max_examples=30`) is CI-affordable.
+- The `user-id` header ENV=local bypass + lifespan stub proved re-usable —
+  future routers are drop-in.
+
+Next-step recommendations (not part of this PoC, out of scope):
+
+1. Fix the Class A unpack bug at `models/assistant.py:1070`.
+2. Add the schemathesis dev-dep + lock to a separate MR once the
+   `codemie-enterprise` registry auth question is resolved
+   (see "Follow-ups" below).
+3. Roll the test module to `datasources`, then to remaining non-LLM
+   routers, one MR per router.
+4. Add a separate CI job (external devops repo) that runs
+   `pytest tests/**/test_schemathesis_*.py --junitxml=...`.
+   Start informational; flip to blocking after two consecutive
+   clean weeks.
+
+---
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- **`schemathesis` dev-dep not committed**: `pyproject.toml` + `poetry.lock`
+  changes were reverted from this branch. Reason: adding the dep required
+  regenerating the lock, which requires auth to the `codemie-enterprise`
+  GCP artifact registry (not configured locally). A follow-up MR should
+  add the dep in an environment that has the registry auth. The PoC test
+  module runs against a locally-installed `schemathesis` in the poetry venv
+  for now.
+- **Class A fix**: file a separate defect ticket referencing
+  `models/assistant.py:1070`.
+- **Class B triage**: file a defect against the MCP loader for
+  `Failed to load MCP tools from 'CLI MCP Server' - ValueError`.
+- **Class D quantification**: rerun after Class A is fixed to see how many
+  endpoints actually violate `response_schema_conformance`.
+- **schemathesis version pin**: `~4.10` is the last minor that supports
+  `pytest 8`. Upgrading to `~4.14` (or newer) requires pinning `pytest ^9`
+  first — a repo-wide change out of scope for this PoC.
+
+---
+
+## Deliverables in this branch
+
+Committed:
+
+- `tests/codemie/rest_api/routers/test_schemathesis_assistants.py` — the test module
+- `.gitignore` — `tests/reports/` entry
+- `docs/superpowers/tasks/2026-07-29-epmcdme-13772-schemathesis-poc/` — spec, plan, technical-analysis, complexity-assessment, red-baseline, first-real-run, findings, and decision log
+
+Not committed (see Follow-ups):
+
+- `pyproject.toml` `schemathesis = "~4.10"` entry
+- `poetry.lock` regenerated with schemathesis
