+Schemathesis PoC — first meaningful run
+========================================
+
+Command:
+    ENV=local poetry run pytest \
+        tests/codemie/rest_api/routers/test_schemathesis_assistants.py \
+        -v --tb=short --junitxml=tests/reports/schemathesis-junit.xml
+
+Duration: 426.44s (0:07:06)  (max_examples=30, 49 endpoints collected)
+
+Result: 42 failed, 7 passed
+
+Endpoints that PASSED (7):
+- (implicit — the diff between 49 collected and 42 failed; not explicitly logged)
+
+Endpoints that FAILED (42) — full list in red-baseline.txt
+
+Wiring verified:
+- Schema loaded from /openapi.json via schemathesis.openapi.from_asgi
+- Path include /v\d+/assistants + exclude (chat|agent|evaluate|ask|enterprise) — 49 endpoints selected out of the assistants router surface (LLM/agent routes correctly filtered out)
+- Custom openapi() override at src/codemie/rest_api/main.py:743 was consumed without error
+- Lifespan stub (no-op async CM) prevented IDP/LiteLLM/Redis startup patches from being needed
+- `user-id: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000` header reached handlers (7 PASSes require auth to have worked)
+
+Sampled failure reasons (via smaller diagnostic runs, tb=short + JUnit XML):
+
+1. `POST /v1/assistants/virtual/model` — Server error (not_a_server_error check)
+   Root cause: schemathesis-generated payload → handler → pydantic serializer
+   receives MagicMock for `single_usage: bool` (some dep unmocked)
+   → serializer warning + downstream failure
+
+2. `DELETE /v1/assistants/{assistant_id}` (and ~10 sibling endpoints with
+   {assistant_id} path param) — Server error via
+   `ValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected 2, got 0)`
+   at src/codemie/rest_api/models/assistant.py:1070
+   Root cause: `Assistant.get_by_id(random_uuid)` returns empty query result
+   `()`, code destructures with `assistant, display_name = result` → crash.
+   Should either return None (caller wraps in 404) or raise NotFoundError.
+   Reproducer curl printed in the failure output:
+       curl -X POST -H 'user-id: 00000000-...' \
+           http://localhost/v1/assistants/0/reactions
+
+3. `POST /v1/assistants/refine` — Pydantic serializer warning:
+   `parsed` field on `RefineGeneratorResponse` receives an unexpected
+   union member; declared as `Optional[<none>]` but the value is a
+   populated model. Schema drift / declared-type mismatch.
+
+4. `GET /v1/assistants/tools`, `/hedgeable_tools`, `/plugin_tools`,
+   `POST /v1/assistants/mcp_tools` — Server errors, several via the
+   MCP tools loader path. Example error body:
+       {"error":{"message":"Assistant Error",
+                 "details":"Failed to load MCP tools from
+                    'CLI MCP Server' - ValueError",
+                 "help":"..."}}
+   The `{"error":{...}}` envelope diverges from FastAPI default
+   `{"detail":...}` — response_schema_conformance would flag this for
+   error paths if the OpenAPI spec doesn't declare the envelope.
+
+5. All 5 category endpoints
+   (GET|POST|PUT|DELETE /v1/assistants/categories/*) — Server errors.
+   Root cause pattern matches #2 (get_by_id / find_by_id unpack on empty
+   result) — same class of finding across CRUD family.
+
+Note: 42/49 failed is a large number; deduplicated by ROOT CAUSE the
+findings collapse to ~4 distinct classes below (see findings.md).
+This is a legitimate signal, not "noise" — one fuzzer run surfaced a
+systemic "empty DB result crashes the handler" bug replicated across
+the assistants router CRUD surface.
