+# Schemathesis PoC — Spec
+
+**Ticket**: [EPMCDME-13772](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMCDME-13772)
+**Story**: `docs/stories/2026-07-29-schemathesis-poc.md`
+**Parent**: EPMCDME-13739 (quality-gates hardening umbrella)
+**Replaces API-level portion of**: EPMCDME-13754
+
+---
+
+## Goal
+
+Prove that Schemathesis can find real contract/5xx bugs in the CodeMie FastAPI backend at acceptable noise levels, by running one narrow property-based test suite against the `assistants` router using the auto-generated OpenAPI schema.
+
+Success = decision at end of PoC: **expand** to remaining routers, or **archive** with a note that OpenAPI + Pydantic already enforce the contract at this level.
+
+---
+
+## Scope
+
+**In**:
+- `tests/codemie/rest_api/routers/test_schemathesis_assistants.py` — one pytest module, ~30–50 LOC
+- `schemathesis` added as a Poetry dev dependency
+- `.gitignore`: `tests/reports/`
+- Local `pytest --junitxml=tests/reports/schemathesis-junit.xml` produces a machine-readable report
+
+**Out**:
+- CI job wiring (lives in external devops repo — out-of-band)
+- Rolling to other routers
+- Stateful / OpenAPI-`links`-following testing
+- Fuzzing LLM / agent / enterprise routes
+- Full production-parity lifespan mocking
+- Sonar push for the report
+- Replacing pure-helper hypothesis tests (that part of EPMCDME-13754 stays independent)
+
+---
+
+## Design decisions
+
+### 1. Router: `assistants`
+
+Chosen because its CRUD surface is DB-only. LLM-invoking endpoints (`ask_*`, `evaluate_*`) are named consistently and can be excluded via one path regex. `datasources` was the alternative but pulls Elasticsearch as an extra mock dependency.
+
+### 2. App entry: `from codemie.rest_api.main import app` + `schemathesis.from_asgi(app)`
+
+Direct import of the FastAPI `app` object. `from_asgi` reads `/openapi.json` from the app itself — no running server, no HTTP client, no network. Custom `openapi()` override at `src/codemie/rest_api/main.py:743` continues to serve the schema; the fuzzer sees the same schema clients would.
+
+### 3. Lifespan: stub, not full
+
+`app.router.lifespan_context` is monkeypatched to a no-op `@asynccontextmanager` for the duration of the schemathesis test session. Rationale: the PoC targets schema-contract violations, not startup integration. Full lifespan requires patching IDP, LiteLLM, Redis scheduler bootstrap, and superadmin seed — 4–6 patches whose failure surfaces would drown out the actual findings.
+
+Trade-off accepted: handlers that depend on state populated during startup (e.g., a Redis-cached lookup) will 5xx. Those are legitimate `not_a_server_error` findings for the PoC — real fragility that a production request would also hit under a cold Redis. If they turn into pure noise, the fix is filter or state-seed in a follow-up, not full lifespan.
+
+### 4. Test placement: inside `tests/codemie/rest_api/routers/`
+
+The existing `tests/codemie/rest_api/routers/conftest.py` disables the rate limiter and injects `request.state.uuid`. Both are prerequisites for any router call to succeed. Living inside that directory inherits both without duplication. A standalone `tests/schemathesis/` would need to re-declare identical fixtures — future drift risk.
+
+### 5. Auth: `user-id` header ENV=local bypass
+
+`ENV=local` is already set for the pytest run (via existing test setup). `PersistentUserProvider` recognises the `USER_ID_HEADER` (see `security/user.py:24`) and calls `authenticate_dev_header(dev_user_id)`, bypassing IDP/JWT. Schemathesis attaches the header to every generated request via a `hook` or `auth` override. UUID is a seeded superadmin (fixture-owned; not hard-coded in the test file).
+
+Note: this corrects the story's original wording ("Bearer via ENV=local hijack"). The mechanism is a header injection, not a Bearer token.
+
+### 6. Checks
+
+Registered exactly three:
+- `not_a_server_error` — no 5xx from any generated input
+- `response_schema_conformance` — response body matches its declared schema
+- `content_type_conformance` — response Content-Type matches OpenAPI
+
+No custom checks in the PoC.
+
+### 7. Endpoint exclusion filter
+
+Schemathesis honours `--exclude-path-regex`. Applied at the module level (not per-endpoint) — one regex covers LLM/agent/enterprise paths that a fuzzer must never hit:
+
+```
+(?i)(chat|agent|evaluate|ask|enterprise|assistant.*(ask|evaluate))
+```
+
+Any endpoint that survives this filter and is *still* backed by an LLM call will surface itself immediately (real API call, real cost) — a bug in the filter, and one worth catching.
+
+### 8. `max_examples = 30`
+
+Small enough to stay under a couple of minutes locally. Large enough to be non-trivial (30 × ~10 endpoints ≈ 300 requests per suite run).
+
+### 9. Report: JUnit XML
+
+`pytest --junitxml=tests/reports/schemathesis-junit.xml`. `tests/reports/` is gitignored. External devops CI picks it up as a build artifact. Sonar integration deferred.
+
+### 10. Success signal
+
+**≥3 distinct classes of findings** across (schema drift | 5xx | content-type mismatch) in the first non-trivial run. A repeated single class (e.g., every error response uses `{"error":...}` shape) counts as one class, not N.
+
+If <3 classes after tuning → archive with the note: "OpenAPI + Pydantic already enforce the contract at this level; property-based coverage is redundant here."
+
+---
+
+## Test file shape
+
+```python
+# tests/codemie/rest_api/routers/test_schemathesis_assistants.py
+import contextlib
+import schemathesis
